  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 124 AM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nThere could be some light sprinkles early this morning over south \ncentral SD lingering behind a cold front that pushed through last \nnight. Other than these sprinkles, high surface pressure will be \nmoving over SD today through Wednesday. This high pressure will help \nto keep rain and storms chances out of central and northeastern SD \nthrough Wednesday. The wildfire smoke that moved in yesterday has \nbeen slowly pushed south by the northerly winds behind the cold \nfront. There might be some lingering light concentrations of smoke \nat the surface early this morning which will be pushed south out of \ncentral and northeastern SD during the morning. There will continue \nto be some wildfire smoke aloft into Wednesday, which could create \nsome hazy skies at times. \n\nThe lingering colder air that was pushed into SD by the cold front \nwill continue to keep temperatures today 5 to 15 degrees colder than \nnormal for this time of the year. Highs across central and \nnortheastern SD and west central MN will be in the 70s with lows \ntonight dropping into the 50s. While the minimum relative humidity \nthis afternoon gets down into the low to mid 20s over north central \nSD, weaker winds only gusting up to 20 mph will help to keep the \nfire weather concerns lower. \n\nA somewhat flat upper-level ridge will be moving in over SD \nWednesday through the rest of the week. This ridge will help to push \na little bit warmer air into SD, causing temperatures to rise back \nup to be around normal. Highs will rise into the 80s then the low \n90s over central SD Wednesday into the weekend, with northeastern SD \nin the upper 70s to 80s. Models hint at a couple of small upper-\nlevel shortwaves that move over SD Thursday and onward. This could \ncause a few surface boundaries to move over the state as well as the \nnext chance for some scattered showers. While the models hint that \nThursday night might see some rain, there is variation in the models \nas to if any of this happens. These potential shortwaves and showers \nwill need to have an eye kept on them to see if models start to come \nto an agreement over the next few days.",
